  "title": "Preview safety fixes: Git variables, consent binding, cleanup removal",
  "body": "Safety fixes for the unqualified preview. Not a qualification.\n\n## Fixes\n- **Inherited Git variables are ignored (P75, P77, P78).** Git's repository-local variables (`git rev-parse --local-env-vars`, matched without case) are now dropped in four places: the kernel process, `GitCli`, the bench fixtures and the privacy check. Before, an inherited `GIT_DIR` or `GIT_WORK_TREE` could point any of them at another repository. Test: `git-env.test.ts`; two of its cases fail without the fix.\n- **Dirty-file answers cover only the files shown (P47, in part).** The answer is refused if the set of files changed after the question, and the question now names every file instead of \"and N more\". Test: `dirty-overlap-bind.test.ts`; it fails without the fix.\n- **A declined hook question is asked again (P48).** After you decline it, a later explicit `commit` asks again instead of running the hook. Test in `workflows.test.ts`; it ran and passed on ubuntu and macOS CI.\n- **Cleanup removal is disabled (P30).** `decide cleanup` still shows the preview of what it would remove, but a confirmed removal is refused with `capability-missing`. Test: `cleanup-disabled.test.ts`.\n\nREADME, skill and CHANGELOG are updated to match.\n\n## CI on `cb104ac`\n- `untrusted` passes on ubuntu, macOS and windows-portability.\n- `system-budgets` still fails on NFR-01 frozen fixtures, unchanged by this PR.\n\n## Still open\n- Recovery and attribution defects (P61, P65).\n- The missing \"wait\" and \"leave this file out\" dirty-file choices.\n- NFR-01 timing.\n- Real-host use.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
